# Benchmark: contains on 5,000 numeric items
# Workload: build a list of 5,000 numbers, then 2 lookups of the LAST item (the
# worst case: every element is compared). Measures equality-driven list scans on
# a list large enough to feel slow. The list build is included; see
# docs/OTTER_1_0_PERFORMANCE_BASELINE.md for the build-only cost.

numbers are empty
count from 1 to 5000 as n
    add n to numbers
.

hits is 0
repeat 2 times
    if numbers contains 5000
        hits is hits plus 1
    .
.
say "contains 5000" hits
